                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "233041960",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198401314165",
                            "num_reviews": 36,
                            "playtime_forever": 355,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 355,
                            "last_played": 1786965238
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This game is worth recommending for the achievement showcase, especially since it’s one of those titles that lets you unlock alphabet achievements you can use to customize your Steam profile. Beyond that, it delivers exactly what you’d expect for its price.\r\n\r\nThe gameplay is very straightforward: simply drive continuously for about 90 minutes and you’ll complete the game. It’s easy overall, but there’s a catch — if you lose in the final minute, you’ll have to restart from the beginning. The soundtrack adds to the experience with a retro vibe that fits the theme nicely.\r\n\r\nWhile playing, I couldn’t help but imagine a scene straight out of The Transporter: a tense car chase with a bomb strapped to the vehicle. Just like in the movie, you can’t slow down too much or speed up too fast — otherwise, it’s game over. That constant balance of speed gives the game its unique tension, even within its simple mechanics.\r\n\r\n",
